$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method A: Suzuki Coupling. A suspension of
bromide (1.0 equiv), boride (0.8 −1.2 equiv), sodium carbonate (4.1 −5.0
mmol), and tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (0) (0.05 equiv) in
dimethoxyethane/water (3:1) was stirred at 90 °C under nitrogen for 2 h.
The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature slowly and then
diluted with water. The aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc, and the
combined organic layers were washed with brine twice and dried over
MgSO4. After evaporation in vacuo, the resulting residue was purified by
flash chromatography to afford the corresponding product.
1-Acety5-(5-fluoropyridin-3-yl)-2,3-dihydro-1 H-indole (18). The title
compound was synthesized according to method A using 17a (150 mg, 0.52
mmol), 3-bromo-5-fluoropyridine (111 mg, 0.63 mmol), sodium carbonate
(277 mg, 2.61 mmol), and tetrakis- (triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (30
mg, 0.03 mmol) in dimethoxyethane (9 mL) and water (3 mL). The crude
product was purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel
(MeOH/CH2Cl2, 0 to 2%) and crystallization from acetone to yield
colorless crystals (108 mg, 81%). mp 178 −180 °C. Rf = 0.26 (MeOH/CH2Cl2,
1:20). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 2.26 (s, 3H), 3.28 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H),
4.13 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.40 (m, 2H), 7.56 (dt, J = 2.0, 9.6 Hz, 1H),
8.30 (d, J = 8.2 Hz,1H), 8.41 (d, J = 1.8 Hz,1H), 8.64 (s, 1H). 13C NMR
(125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 24.2, 27.9, 49.0, 117.4, 118.1, 120.7 (d, 2JC,F =
18.6 Hz), 123.2, 126.8, 131.5, 132.3, 136.0 (d, 2JC,F = 23.3 Hz), 138.1
(d, 4J C,F = 3.6 Hz), 143.6 (d, 4JC,F = 3.2 Hz), 159.7 (d, 1JC,F = 257
Hz), 168.9. MS (ESI) m/z = 257 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
