$DATUM Copolymer P1. To a mixture of 4,7-bis(boronic acid pinacol
ester)-2,1,3-benzothiadiazole (7, 0.15 mmol, 58.2 mg),
2,8-dibromo-4,6-di-n-dodecylbenzo[2,1-b:3,4-b':5,6-c'']trithiophene (6,
0.15 mmol, 111.1 mg), aliquat 336 (15 μmol, 6.0 mg,), and Pd(PPh3)4 (2.3
mg, 2.0 μmol) under argon was added 2M aqueous K2CO3 (2.0 mL) and toluene
(6.0 mL). The mixture was heated at 90 °C for 72 h with vigorously
stirring. The polymer was end-capped with phenyl by adding phenylboronic
acid and bromobenzene in sequence. After cooling to room temperature, the
reaction mixture was diluted in chloroform. The organic phase was washed
with brine and dried with MgSO4. After removal of the solvent, the
residue was dissolved with a minimum amount of chloroform and
precipitated in methanol. The polymer was filtered and subjected to
Soxhlet extraction with acetone (24 h), hexane (24 h) and chloroform (24
h). The chloroform fraction was concentrated and precipitated into
methanol. Following filtration, the purified polymer was obtained.
Solid-state 13C {1H} CP MAS spectra with different contact times. Yield:
(86 mg, 80%). Deep purple solid. GPC: Mn = 19.5 kg/mol; Mw = 38.6 kg/mol;
PDI = 1.98. λabsmax (nm) (soln): 547 (1 × 10-5 M), ε: 11400 M-1cm-1,
film: 570.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Benzotrithiophene-Based Donor-Acceptor Copolymers with Distinct
Supramolecular Organizations
