$DATUM 2-Chloro-5-methyl-4-(thiophen-2-yl)pyrimidine (3). A mixture of
2,4-dichloro-5-methylpyrimidine (2) (2.10 g, 15.4 mmol),
thiophene-2-boronic acid (1.98 g, 15.4 mmol), potassium carbonate (6.42
g, 46.4 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (1.79 g, 1.54 mmol) and DME (39 mL) in a sealed
tube was allowed to stir at 110 °C for 20 h. Upon completion, the mixture
was filtered and the precipitate was washed with CH2Cl2. The combined
organic phases were washed with 2N aqueous HCl solution, water, aqueous
saturated sodium bicarbonate solution and brine, dried over anhydrous
sodium sulfate and concentrated. The residue was purified by column
chromatography using 10% EtOAc/hexane as the eluent. 3 (2.10 g, 80%). 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD) δ = 8.46 (s, 1H), 7.90 (dd, J = 3.9, 1.2 Hz, 1H),
7.77 (dd, J = 5.1, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.26 (dd, J = 5.1, 3.9 Hz, 1H), 2.56 (s,
3H). LCMS (ES+) m/z 211 (M+H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal, Suzuki coupling, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Potent and Orally Bioavailable GPR142 Agonists as Novel Insulin
Secretagogues for the Treatment of Type 2 Diabetes
