$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of 11, 12 and 13. A mixture of the
thienylboronic ester (3 mmol), 10 (1 mmol), PdCl2dppf (0.05 mmol) and
NaHCO3 (2 mmol) in THF/water 2:1 (3 mL) was irradiated with microwaves at
80°C for 15 min. The reaction mixture was brought to room temperature and
the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure. The octamers (11, 12,
13) were isolated by flash chromatography with increasing amounts of
CH2Cl2 in cyclohexane as eluent.
5,5'''''''-Dihexyl-3''',3''''',4'',4''''-tetrakis(hexylsulphanyl)-octithiophene
(12). Yield 80%. Purple-red powder. mp 95-97°C; TLC (cyclohexane:CH2Cl2,
85:15 v/v): Rf = 0.48; 1H NMR (400 MHz, C6D6): δ 7.28 (s, 2H), 7.19 (s,
2H), 6.88 (d, 3J=3.6 Hz, 2H), 6.84 (d, 3J=3.6 Hz, 2H), 6.81(d, 3J=3.6 Hz,
2H), 6.65 (d, 3J=3.6 Hz, 2H), 2.64 (q, J=7.2 Hz, 8H), 2.51 (t, 4H),
1.50-1.45 (m, 12H), 1.20-1.03 (m, 36H), 0.85-0.78 (m, 18H); 13C NMR (400
MHz, C6D6): δ 145.9, 138.1, 137.6, 136.6, 135.0, 134.96, 133.55, 133.53,
132.9, 131.9, 127.5, 125.4, 125.35, 124.2, 124.1, 36.6, 36.58, 31.9,
31.89, 31.71, 31.70, 30.4, 29.9, 29.8, 29.0, 28.75, 28.73, 23.0, 14.32,
14.31, 14.29; UV/Vis: λmax 433 nm, λem. 570 nm in CH2Cl2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, microwave irradiation (100 W), Suzuki coupling, sealed
glass vessel used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Successful Chemical Strategy To Induce Oligothiophene Self-Assembly
into Fibers with Tunable Shape and Function
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Di Maria, Francesca; Olivelli, Pasquale; Gazzano, Massimo; Zanelli,
Alberto; Biasiucci, Mariano; Gigli, Giuseppe; Gentili, Denis; D'Angelo,
Pasquale; Cavallini, Massimiliano; Barbarella, Giovanna
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2011), 133(22), 8654-8661

