$DATUM 3-(2,2'-Bithien-5-yl)-4,4'-difluoro-2,6-dimethyl-5-(thien-2-yl)-4-bora-3a,4a-diaza-s-indacene
(8a). 2a (50 mg, 0.11 mmol, 1 equiv), cesium carbonate (108 mg, 0.33
mmol, 3 equiv) and 5a (25 mg, 0.12 mmol, 1.1 equiv) were dissolved in
toluene (6 mL) in a Schlenk flask and degassed for 30 min. Then Pd(PPh3)4
(13 mg, 0.011 mmol, 0.1 equiv) was added and the solution was heated to
60 °C. The reaction was monitored by TLC inspection. After 18 h the
reaction was hydrolyzed, extracted with CH2Cl2 and dried over MgSO4. The
solvent was removed under vacuum. The residue was purified by column
chromatography (SiO2, petroleum ether/CH2Cl2 70:30 to 60:40) and
recrystallized from CH2Cl2/EtOH. The compound 8a was obtained. Blue
metallic crystals, yield 41 mg, 80%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, ppm): δ =
7.78 (m, 2H), 7.52 (d, 3J = 5.0 Hz, 1H), 7.25 (m, 2H), 7.22 (d, 3J = 4.0
Hz, 1H), 7.17 (dd, 3J = 3.8 Hz, 3J = 5.0 Hz, 1H), 7.03 (dd, 3J = 4.0 Hz,
3J = 4.5 Hz, 1H), 6.97 (s, 1H), 6.84 (s, 2H), 2.29 (s, 3H), 2.23 (s, 3H);
13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, ppm): δ = 149.7, 149.2, 141.0, 136.8, 135.2,
134.9, 133.0 (t, JC-F = 6.9 Hz), 132.3, 131.7 (t, JC-F = 5.5 Hz), 131.2,
130.45, 130.36, 129.6, 129.2, 128.8, 128.0, 127.9, 127.6, 125.2, 124.6,
124.4, 124.2, 13.9, 13.5; 11B NMR (128 MHz, CDCl3, ppm): δ = 1.32 (t, 1J
= 33.9 Hz); UV-vis (CH2Cl2) λ nm (ε, M-1m-1): 626 (57000), 357 (23000),
302 (18000), 223 (24000); IR (ν, cm-1): 3110, 3070, 2952, 2918, 1592,
1529, 1500, 1443, 1398; EI-MS m/z (nature of the peak, relative
intensity): 466.0 ([M]+, 100); Anal. Calcd for C23H17BF2N2S3: C, 59.23;
H, 3.67; N, 6.01. Found: C, 58.98; H, 3.51; N, 5.64.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Oligothienyl-BODIPYs: Red and Near-Infrared Emitters
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
