$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Compounds 2e-2u and 2ak-2am by
Suzuki Reaction. General Procedure. To a solution of the appropriate
bromoquinolone 7 or iodoquinolone 2a (1 mmol) in DME (4 mL), Pd(OAc)2(0.1
mmol), PPh3 (0.3 mmol), the appropriate boronic acid (0.5 mmol), EtOH (1
mL), and 1 N Na2CO3 (2 mL) were added. The mixture was irradiated with
microwaves at 150 °C for 10 min, then filtered through a plug of Celite.
The filtrate was washed with H2O, brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and
evaporated to dryness. The solid residue was purified by flash
chromatography using CH2Cl2 /MeOH (98:2) as eluent.
N-(Adamntan-1-yl)-6-(5-chlorothiophen-2-yl)-4-oxo-1-pentyl-1,4-dihydroquinoline-3-carboxamide
2l. 80% yield. Yellow solid. Mp 181-182°C. 1HNMR (200 MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.87
(s, 1H), 8.69 (s, 1H), 8.60 (d, J = 2.1 Hz, 1H), 7.80 (dd, J1 = 2.1, J2 =
8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.53 d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.18 (d, J = 4.0 Hz, 1H), 6.89 (d,
J = 4.0 Hz, 1H), 4.19 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 2.16 (s, 6H), 2.09 (s, 3H),
1.94-1.79 (m, 2H), 1.78-1.70 (m, 6H), 1.36-1.22 (m, 4H), 0.88 (t, J = 6.8
Hz, 3H). MS (ESI): m/z: 510[M+H]+ 532[M+Na]+. IR (CHCl3): υ1601, 1656
cm-1. Anal.(C29H33ClN2O2S), C, H, N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Investigations on the 4-Quinolone-3-carboxylic Acid Motif. 3. Synthesis,
Structure-Affinity Relationships, and Pharmacological Characterization of
6-Substituted 4-Quinolone-3-carboxamides as Highly Selective
Cannabinoid-2 Receptor Ligands
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pasquini, Serena; Ligresti, Alessia; Mugnaini, Claudia; Semeraro, Teresa;
