$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of 11, 12
and 13. A mixture of the thienylboronic ester (3 mmol), 10 (1 mmol),
PdCl2dppf (0.05 mmol) and NaHCO3 (2 mmol) in THF/water 2:1 (3 mL) was
irradiated with microwaves at 80°C for 15 min. The reaction mixture was
brought to room temperature and the solvent was evaporated under reduced
pressure. The octamers (11, 12, 13) were isolated by flash chromatography
with increasing amounts of CH2Cl2 in cyclohexane as eluent.
3''',3''''',4'',4'''',5,5'''''''-Hexakis(hexylsulphanyl)-octithiophene
(13). Yield 80%. Purple-red powder. mp 85-87°C; TLC (cyclohexane:CH2Cl2,
85:15 v/v): Rf = 0.38; 1H NMR (400 MHz, C6D6): δ 7.28 (s, 2H), 7.18 (s,
2H), 6.83 (d, 3J=3.6 Hz, 2H), 6.78 (d, 3J=3.6 Hz, 2H), 6.75 (d, 3J=3.6
Hz, 2H), 6.72 (d, 3J=3.6 Hz, 2H), 2.64 (q, J=6.8 Hz, 8H), 2.56 (t, 4H),
1.49-1.44 (m, 12H), 1.21-1.12 (m, 24H), 1.08-1.03 (m, 12H), 0.82-0.77 (m,
18H); 13C NMR (400 MHz, C6D6): δ 140.1, 137.1, 136.8, 136.5, 135.6,
135.4, 134.2, 133.5, 133.4, 132.6, 132.1, 125.2, 124.8, 124.2, 38.9,
36.44, 36.42, 31.53, 31.51, 31.47, 29.7, 29.6, 28.6, 28.5, 28.3, 22.8,
22.7, 14.11, 14.10, 14.06; UV/Vis: λmax 434 nm, λem. 560 nm in CH2Cl2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, microwave irradiation (100 W), Suzuki coupling, sealed
glass vessel used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Successful Chemical Strategy To Induce Oligothiophene Self-Assembly
into Fibers with Tunable Shape and Function
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
