$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2,4-Diamino-5-(furan-2-yl)-7-(β
-D-ribofuranosyl)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine (8a). An argon-purged
mixture of 2,4-diamino-5-iodo-7-(β-
D-ribofuranosyl)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine 2729 (305 mg, 0.75 mmol),
furan-2-boronic acid (126 mg, 1.125 mmol), Na2CO3 (239 mg, 2.25 mmol),
Pd(OAc)2 (8 mg, 0.036 mmol), and TPPTS (53 mg, 0.093 mmol) in water/MeCN
(2:1, 5 mL) was stirred at 100 °C for 3 h. After cooling, the mixture was
neutralized using aq HCl (1 M) and concentrated to dryness in vacuo, and
the residue was purified by reverse phase HPFC (C-18, 0→ 100% MeOH in
water) to afford 8a which was crystallized from water.
2,4-Diamino-5-(benzofuran-2-yl)-7-(β
-D-ribofuranosyl)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3-d]pyrimidine (8f). Compound 8f was
prepared as described for 8a from 27 (305 mg, 0.75 mmol) and
benzofuran-2-boronic acid as a redish glassy solid (238 mg, 80%). Mp
142-144 °C. [α ]D -69.4 (c 0.311, DMSO). 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6): 3.54
(ddd, 1H, Jgem = 11.9 Hz, J5´a,OH = 6.0 Hz, J5´a,4´ = 4.1 Hz, H-5´a);
3.63 (ddd, 1H, Jgem = 11.9 Hz, J5´b,OH = 5.3 Hz, J5´b,4´ = 4.0 Hz,
H-5´b); 3.86 (td, 1H, J4´,5´a = J4´,5´b = 4.0 Hz, J4´,3´ = 3.3 Hz, H-4´);
4.09 (td, 1H, J3´,2´ = J3´,OH = 4.9 Hz, J3´,4´ = 3.3 Hz, H-3'); 4.38 (td,
1H, J2´,1´ = J2´,OH = 6.3 Hz, J2´,3´ = 5.2 Hz, H-2'); 5.10 (d, 1H, JOH,3´
= 4.6 Hz, OH-3´); 5.18 (bt, 1H, JOH,5´a = OH,5´b = 5.7 Hz, OH-5´); 5.32
(d, 1H, JOH,2´ = 6.3 Hz, OH-2´); 5.84 (bs, 2H, NH2-2); 6.00 (d, 1H,
J1´,2´ = 6.4 Hz, H-1'); 6.55 (bs, 2H, NH2-4); 7.03 (d, 1H, J3,7 = 1.0 Hz,
H-3-benzofuryl); 7.23 - 7.29 (m, 2H, H-5,6-benzofuryl); 7.58 - 7.65 (m,
2H, H-4,7-benzofuryl); 7.68 (s, 1H, H-6). 13C NMR (125.7 MHz, DMSO-d6):
61.92 (CH2-5´); 70.79 (CH-3'); 73.63 (CH-2'); 85.02 (CH-4'); 86.30
