$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of 66 (2.37 g, 6.15 mmol), 125 (1.89 g, 6.83 mmol),
Pd(Amphos)2Cl2 (224 mg, 0.32 mmol), and KOAc (2.72 g, 27.7 mmol) was
suspended in EtOH (30 mL) and H2O (7.5 mL). N2 was bubbled through the
suspension for about 20 s, and the mixture was then heated at 88 °C for
2.75 h. The reaction was allowed to cool to 22 °C, treated with H2O (90
mL), and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 100 mL). The combined organic
extracts were dried (Na2SO4), filtered, concentrated, and purified by
silica gel column chromatography (gradient: 80% CH2Cl2/hexanes → CH2Cl2 →
3.5% MeOH/ CH2Cl2) to give
4-(2-fluoro-5-(4-(methylthio)benzyl)pyridin-3-yl)-N,N-bis(4-methoxybenzyl)-6-methyl-1,3,5-triazin-2-amine
(126). Yield (2.84 g, 80%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.32 (dd, J = 9.00
Hz, 2.35 Hz, 1H), 8.14 (dd, J = 1.56 Hz, 1H), 7.24- 7.18 (m, 6H),
7.13-7.09 (m, 2H), 6.90-6.83 (m, 4H), 4.81 (s, 2H), 4.78 (s, 2H), 3.99
(s, 2H), 3.82 (s, 3H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 2.53 (s, 3H), 2.46 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
