$DATUM 142-82-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of
5-bromo-1-methyl-3-[5-(4-methyl-piperazin-1-yl)-pyridin-2-ylamino]-1H-pyridin-2-one
(200 g, 529 mmol), bis(pinacolato)diboron (161 g, 634 mmol), Pd(OAc)2
(2.85g, 13.2 mmol), X-Phos (7.57 g, 15.8 mmol), KOAc (242 g, 2470 mmol),
and dioxane (1200 mL) was stirred and degassed three times. The mixture
was heated at 100° C for 2 hours then cooled to 65°C. The slurry was
filtered through a pad of celite (100 g). The cake was washed with 800 mL
of dioxane and the filtrate was distilled under vacuum to 800 mL. The
residue was heated to 65°C. Heptane (1200 mL) was slowly added over 1 h.
The slurry was cooled to room temperature and further cooled in an ice
bath for 4 hours. The product was isolated by filtration and washed with
a mixed solution of heptane (500 mL) and dioxane (250 mL) that had been
pre-cooled to 0°C. The cake was dried overnight in a 70°C. vacuum oven.
The product, 1-methyl-3-[S-(4-methyl-piperazin-1-yl)-pyridin-2-ylamino
5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-[1 ,3,2]dioxaborolan-2-yl)-IH-pyridin-2-one, was
obtained as a brown solid (178g, 79% yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structure-Based Drug Design of RN486, a Potent and Selective Bruton's
Tyrosine Kinase (BTK) Inhibitor, for the Treatment of Rheumatoid
Arthritis
