$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: S8-7.
2-(5-(5-(HBQA-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)-5,5-dimethyl-1,3-dioxane
(8) To a stirred solution of 2 (0.22 g, 0.49 mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (0.028
g, 0.024 mmol) in tetrahydrofuran (10 mL) was added
4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-2-(5-(5-(5,5-dimethyl-1,3-dioxan-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
(0.89 g, 2.19 mmol), potassium carbonate (2.76 g, 20 mmol) in THF (15 mL)
and H2O (10 mL). The mixture was refluxed for 18 h. After cooling the
solution, H2O (30 ml) was added to the solution and extracted by
dichloromethane (30 mL × 3). The organic layer was separated and dried in
MgSO4. The solvent was removed in vacuo. The pure product 8 was obtained
by silica gel chromatography using a mixture of methylene chloride and
n-hexane (1:1) as an eluent. S8-9.
2-(5-(5-(6,10-Dinonyl-HBQA-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)-5,5-dimethyl-1,3-dioxane
(10) The product was synthesized according to the procedure as described
above for synthesis of 8, giving a yellow solid of the product 10 in 79 %
yield. Mp: 187 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.55 (s, 2H), 7.18 (m, 5H), 7.14 (d,
1H, J = 3.6 Hz), 7.05 (d, 1H, J = 3.6 Hz), 7.01 (d, 1H, J = 3.6 Hz), 5.63
(s, 1H), 3.71 (m, 4H), 2.63 (t, 4H, J = 7.5 Hz), 1.66 (s, 12H), 1.65 (s,
6H), 1.64 (m, 4H), 1.34 - 1.28 (m, 24H), 1.30 (s, 3H), 0.88 (t, 6H, J =
6.9 Hz), 0.81 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 144.2, 139.9, 137.1, 135.4,
132.3, 130.1, 129.8, 129.5, 128.0, 125.9, 124.8, 124.0, 123.5, 122.7,
120.9, 98.3, 77.6, 35.7, 35.5, 34.0, 33.8, 33.1, 32.0, 31.7, 30.3, 29.7,
29.6, 29.5, 29.4, 23.1, 22.8, 21.9, 14.2. MS: m/z 895 [M+]. Anal. Calcd.
for C59H77NO2S2: C, 79.05; H, 8.66. Found: C, 78.99; H, 8.58.
